// Motion Prompt #099 · MIT License (c) 2026 Shohei Ohtaki · https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/#099
//
// Silhouette / シルエット
// Pack: photo (Photo looks, lighting & styles) · element 03 · Category: Lighting & time of day
// What happens: As the exposure is set for the bright evening sky, the person, buildings, lamp and tree turn into flat black shapes with no detail and only the sky stays bright.
// Motion spec:
//   - Scene 1: a head-and-shoulders figure in front of a horizon at y 150 (head centre x 270, y 78, radius 29 px, no face or hair). 
//   - Sky: #FAF9F7 → #FFEDC4 at the top and a #FFCF73 band near the horizon (y 92–150)
//   - Everything but the sky becomes #2A2D36, the far hills #4A4546; the figure #22252D
//   - Sun: radius 20 px at x 404, sinking from y 60 to y 128, half hidden by the hills
//   - Top-right readout: ±0.0 EV → −2.0 EV
//   - Timing: the effect comes in from 0.4 s to 1.4 s, holds until 4.0 s and is gone again by 4.8 s (one pass = 5 s, cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)))
// When to use it: When the shape and pose should carry the picture, against a sunset or a bright window.
// Tags: silhouette, backlit, sunset, contre-jour, black shape, underexposed
// Size: 539x208 px · Cycle: 5 s
// Needs: kit photo -> https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/photo.js
// Live demo: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/#099
//
// cells[i](k, w, h, u): k = CanvasRenderingContext2D (already cleared and wrapped in save/restore by the caller), w,h = size, u = seconds in [0, cycle). The picture depends only on u.
// Element code starts here. CELLS, constants and helpers live in the kit.

// @element 03
// シルエット: 露出を明るい空に合わせると、人物も建物も木も黒い形だけになる
CELLS[2] = cell((k, u) => {
  const a = env(u), INK = '#2A2D36';
  const SILH = mapPal(BASE, () => INK);
  Object.assign(SILH, { sky: '#FFEDC4', sky2: '#FFCF73', far: '#4A4546', sun: BASE.sun, glow: BASE.glow });
  stagePortrait(k, pal(BASE, SILH, a), { sun: [404, lerp(60, 128, a), 20, a] });
  bust(k, PX, PY, PR, mixc(BASE.person, '#22252D', a));
  hud(k, `${(-2 * a).toFixed(1).replace('-0.0', '±0.0')} EV`);
});
